IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nmw-types`
IMPORT `nmw-qualification`
IMPORT `nmw-arrears`
IMPORT `nmw-records`

-- National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "Does this individual qualify for the national minimum wage; how much
--    additional remuneration are they owed for the periods they were
--    underpaid; and, if they asked to see the employer's records, by when
--    must the records be produced, by when must a complaint be presented,
--    and what is the award?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Minimum wage case` HAS
    `the individual`                                    IS A `Qualification facts`
    `the question arises in civil proceedings`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pay reference periods`                         IS A LIST OF `Underpaid period`
    `the records request`                               IS A MAYBE `Records request`

DECLARE `Minimum wage position` HAS
    -- NOTHING when qualification cannot be decided: a condition of s 1(2)
    -- not established, outside civil proceedings (changed after the
    -- independent pass, so that the records fields still answer).
    `qualifies`                                         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `additional remuneration owed`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `last day to produce the records`                   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to present a records complaint`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `records award`                                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 1, 10, 11, 11A, 17, 28, 34-45B, 54
@export default The national minimum wage position under the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) for one individual: whether they qualify (s 1(2), with the exclusions and the s 28(1) presumption in civil proceedings); the additional remuneration owed under s 17 for the pay reference periods in which they were paid less than the national minimum wage (0 if they do not qualify; both NOTHING if, outside civil proceedings, a condition of s 1(2) is not established); and, if they gave a production notice, the last day for the employer to produce the records (s 10(9)), the last day to present a complaint (ss 11(3), 11A) and the award of 80 times the hourly rate on a well-founded complaint (s 11(2)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Minimum wage case`  @desc The individual's qualification facts, whether the question arises in civil proceedings, each pay reference period (hours, remuneration, R1, payments of arrears made) with R2 at the time of determination, and any records request
GIVETH A `Minimum wage position`
`the national minimum wage position for` c MEANS
    `Minimum wage position` WITH
        `qualifies`                                     IS
            IF decidable THEN JUST qualifies ELSE NOTHING
        `additional remuneration owed`                  IS
            IF   decidable
            THEN JUST (IF qualifies THEN `the additional remuneration for all of` (c's `the pay reference periods`) ELSE 0)
            ELSE NOTHING
        `last day to produce the records`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the records request`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the last day to produce the records for` r)
        `last day to present a records complaint`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the records request`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the last day to present a complaint for` r)
        `records award`                                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `the records request`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the s 11 award for` r)
    WHERE
        decidable MEANS `qualification can be decided for` (c's `the individual`) `in civil proceedings` (c's `the question arises in civil proceedings`)
        qualifies MEANS `qualifies for the national minimum wage` (c's `the individual`) `in civil proceedings` (c's `the question arises in civil proceedings`)
